  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global elimination of mercury in non-ferrous metals initiative, global</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">.The GEMINI Program goal is to foster a mercury-free production and supply of non-ferrous metals while disseminating knowledge to facilitate the transition to mercury-free safe alternatives and responsible practices in the nonferrous metals industry. The GEMINI Program framework is designed to help industries and countries meet their environmental commitments on the Minamata Convention, specifically by reducing mercury emissions produced during non-ferrous metal production and by implementing innovative practices and demonstration technologies supported through collaboration and knowledge sharing. The GEMINI Program has 7 Child Projects: Mexico and India implemented by UNDP, South Africa and Brazil implemented by UNEP, and Chile, Peru and Zambia implemented by UNIDO. GEF Global Child Project Grant: 10,000,000.00 USD</narrative>
  </description>
